{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Those were the waters of Merivah.</b> They said in the Midrash: from here you learn that it was decreed at Kadesh that Moses would be punished on account of the waters. See what is written (Genesis 14:7): ״וישובו ויבאו אל עין משפט היא קדש״ — 'they returned and came to Ein Mishpat, that is, Kadesh.' The 'spring of judgment' (עין משפט) of Moses — that is Kadesh, and it was called Kadesh on account of להקדישני — 'to sanctify Me.'" "<b>And He was sanctified through them.</b> Through Moses and Aaron. The measure of the Holy One, blessed be He, is measure for measure: they caused that His name was not sanctified; therefore ויקדש בם — He was sanctified through them, the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, was sanctified upon them, in the manner of what is written (Leviticus 10:3): ״בקרובי אקדש״. And this sin began through Israel and came upon Moses and Aaron inadvertently. Concerning this the verse says (Psalms 106:32): ״ויקציפו על מי מריבה וירע למשה בעבורם״ — 'they provoked Him at the waters of Merivah, and it went ill with Moses on their account.' To what may the matter be compared? To two women being flogged in a court: one had committed a wrong and one had eaten unripe figs of the seventh year. The one who ate unripe figs of the seventh year said to them: I beg you, make it known to the public on what account I am being flogged, so that they do not say, 'I too committed a wrong.' They brought an unripe fig of the seventh year and flogged her. So said Moses, Master of all worlds: You have decreed upon me to die in the wilderness together with the generation that provoked You, as is said (ibid. v. 38): ״כמה ימרוהו במדבר יעציבוהו בישימון״. Write concerning me on account of what I was punished. And it is known that had it not been for the sin of the Rock, they would have entered the Land, for the tribe of Levi is not included in the decree of the wilderness, as it is written (Numbers 14:29): ״וכל פקודיכם לכל מספרכם״, and the tribe of Levi was not numbered among Israel generally but separately on its own."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:18.585502501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}